    "SubTopic": "Factor Theorem",
    "Difficulty": "Olympiad",
    "Explanation": "Statement 1 is FALSE — a degree-n polynomial has at most n real factors; it may have complex roots or repeated factors. For example, x²+1 has no real factors. Statement 2 is TRUE — this is the Factor Theorem: if p(a)=0, then (x-a) divides p(x) exactly."
